schema: "0.4"
id: npl-meridian-24-ticket-board
type: image
quality: high

# NoizuPromptLingo — a structured prompt-definition language + MCP agent toolchain — Ticket Board (kanban) screen.
# Theme tenets: warm espresso-dark surface, single matte-brass accent, verdigris-teal secondary, display-serif titles over Inter body, refined 6px radius, "well-lit study at night".
# Palette: espresso #1a1613 canvas, panel #241f1a, parchment #f2ebe0 text, brass #c9a15e accent, verdigris #3f857e secondary.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity UI mockup of a
    PREMIUM, warm-dark kanban board — a considered ticket board a delivery lead reads
    to see work across stages. The register is refined, calm, composed, with quiet
    gravitas: a well-lit study at night, not a build monitor. Warm low light, matte
    brass detailing, unhurried. Column headers and the board title are a warm
    high-contrast DISPLAY SERIF; card body and labels are a neutral sans; ticket ids
    are monospace. The accent is a single matte, desaturated brass used as a thin line
    or small fill — never a gradient, glow, or gold bling.
  text: |
    A 16:9 high-fidelity UI mockup of the Ticket Board (kanban) screen of
    NoizuPromptLingo, rendered in a warm espresso-dark mode.

    OVERALL LAYOUT (two regions): a slim LEFT NAV RAIL; a wide MAIN COLUMN with a board
    header and a horizontal row of kanban columns.

    LEFT NAV RAIL: warm-charcoal sidebar, "NPL" wordmark in the display serif, a short
    destination list; the active "Tickets" item marked by a thin brass left-rail.

    BOARD HEADER: the board name in a large display-serif heading, a muted subtitle,
    an ITERATION SELECTOR at right (a recessed dropdown chip reading "Sprint 14"), a
    small assignee avatar cluster, and a brass-outlined ghost "Filter" button.

    KANBAN COLUMNS: four warm-charcoal BOARD COLUMNS across the canvas — "Backlog",
    "In Progress", "Review", "Done" — each with a display-serif column header, a small
    count chip beside it, and a faint hairline separating the header from the stack.
    Each column holds 2-4 TICKET CARDS.

    TICKET CARD: a raised warm panel at 6px radius with generous padding — a monospace
    ticket id chip ("NPL-142") at the top, a title line in sans, a thin row of small
    badges (a status tint, an ITERATION badge, and a small assignee avatar), and a
    muted meta line. One card sits in a lifted/hover state showing a soft warm shadow
    and a thin brass hairline; a second card shows a clearly visible 2px BRASS FOCUS
    OUTLINE (keyboard focus) to signal full keyboard navigability. A "+load more"
    pagination affordance sits faint at one column's foot.

    PALETTE & TYPE: every neutral is a warm charcoal (espresso canvas, warmer raised
    cards and columns), never cool slate; text is a soft warm parchment, never pure
    white. The accent is a matte brass/champagne on the focus outline, featured-card
    hairline, active nav rail, and ghost-button outline; muted verdigris teal only on
    links. Iteration and status badges use muted warm tints, never loud brand hues.
    Column headers and board title in the warm display serif; card body in a neutral
    sans; ids in monospace.

    SHAPE & SURFACE: refined 6px radius on cards and columns, 4px on badges; warm tonal
    elevation with a soft warm shadow under the lifted card — no glow. A barely
    perceptible warm radial vignette over the shell, like a single study lamp. Brass is
    a pinstripe and a focus line, never a heavy frame.

    MOOD: refined, composed, quietly premium — a considered board for reading the state
    of work, calm rather than busy, with an obvious accessible focus state.
  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, blurry, distorted UI, cool blue slate tones, neon glow, gold gradient bling, terminal/console green"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Matches Ticket Board: left nav rail, board header with an iteration selector, a horizontal row of kanban columns (Backlog/In Progress/Review/Done) holding ticket cards with id + iteration + assignee badges, a visible keyboard focus ring, and a column pagination affordance"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Warm espresso-dark neutrals (not cool slate), single matte-brass accent (focus outline, hairlines) + verdigris links, display-serif column headers over sans card body, muted warm badge tints, 6px radius"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "Legible multi-column board with a calm, considered rhythm; plausible real kanban"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9 aspect, no artifacts"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"
    - "cool/blue terminal darkness or phosphor-green accent (that is the Nocturne sibling, not Meridian)"

tags: [npl-meridian, NoizuPromptLingo, screen-mockup]
